# .lycheeignore — silence known-flaky external URL patterns for the
# docs-link-check CI tier (story 1.22 AC8). One regex per line; comments
# (lines starting with `#`) and blank lines are ignored by lychee.
#
# Each entry below documents WHY the URL is suppressed. Add new entries
# sparingly — every silenced URL is a link we cannot mechanically verify;
# prefer fixing the link or finding a more stable target before adding here.

# docs.docker.com — install-guide URLs use HTTP redirects between marketing
# and product sub-domains that occasionally 404 mid-chain even when the
# canonical destination is healthy. The links remain present in the docs
# because they are the canonical operator-facing references.
^https://docs\.docker\.com/

# linear.app — public marketing pages (e.g. settings/api landing) sometimes
# bot-block lychee's User-Agent. The URLs are still useful to readers.
^https://linear\.app/

# github.com — silence ONLY JS-rendered heading anchors on `blob/` views
# (lychee's static fetch can't see anchors injected by GitHub's frontend).
# Issue / PR / comment / code-line anchors are NOT covered — those are
# static HTML and should be validated; broken back-references must fail.
^https://github\.com/[^/]+/[^/]+/blob/[^#]+#[A-Za-z0-9_-]+$

# adoptium.net — package-listing pages occasionally rate-limit lychee in CI.
^https://(packages\.|www\.)?adoptium\.net/
